// Every row of the runtime's math table (`runtime/src/math/bits.rs`) through compiled code, one
// result per line, then `sin`, `cos`, `atan2`, `exp`, `log` and `pow` of six `float` inputs (widened
// to `f64`, computed, narrowed once). Printing is the shortest text that reads back as the same
// value, so equal text is equal bits (NaN aside). `print_table` in that file prints these lines.
// Kestrel has no exponent in literals: the long literals are 1e300, 1e22, 1e-300, 1e-310 and the
// smallest subnormal, 5e-324.
